### **Complete order statuses**

| Status             | Meaning                             |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| CART               | Products selected                   |
| CHECKOUT_PENDING   | Checkout in progress                |
| PENDING_PAYMENT    | Payment not yet confirmed           |
| PAYMENT_FAILED     | Payment failed                      |
| CONFIRMED          | Payment/order confirmation complete |
| GROWER_ACCEPTED    | Grower accepted                     |
| PREPARING          | Produce being prepared              |
| READY_FOR_PICKUP   | Order ready                         |
| DELIVERY_ASSIGNING | Finding a delivery partner          |
| DELIVERY_ASSIGNED  | Partner assigned                    |
| PICKED_UP          | Partner collected order             |
| OUT_FOR_DELIVERY   | Order in transit                    |
| DELIVERED          | OTP-verified delivery               |
| CANCELLED          | Order cancelled                     |
| REFUND_PENDING     | Refund being processed              |
| REFUNDED           | Refund completed                    |
| DELIVERY_FAILED    | Delivery attempt unsuccessful       |

Not every order must pass through every status. For example, an unpaid order cannot become a completed order.

### **Critical business rules**

1. A grower cannot accept an order for unavailable stock.
2. A customer cannot pay a different amount from the verified backend amount.
3. A delivery partner cannot pick up an unassigned order.
4. A delivery partner cannot complete an order without valid completion verification.
5. A customer cannot mark a payment successful by editing the frontend.
6. An order cannot be completed twice.
7. Cancellation and refund operations must be idempotent.
8. Every significant status transition must be logged.

