**Three things must not be compromised:**

1. **Real functionality:** No fake payment success, simulated tracking presented as live GPS, imaginary inventory or dummy order completion.
2. **Data security:** No exposed credentials, unauthorized admin access, public customer locations or uncontrolled financial operations.
3. **Operational reliability:** Inventory, payments, seller acceptance, delivery assignment and order status must remain consistent across all applications.

**My final recommendation:** Freeze this as the ZENVEGO master product specification. Develop in phases, preserve working code, and integrate and test each module before moving to the next. Do not keep redesigning the architecture or adding features before the complete order-to-delivery workflow works reliably.